Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.74,0:00:56.42,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,Your Highness, \Nthe Blacksail Fleet has returned.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.42,0:00:59.78,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,They intercepted a merchant fleet \Nfrom Valencia heading to Wolfheart.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.78,0:01:02.08,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,The haul from this trip is substantial,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.08,0:01:04.81,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,enough to arm an entire squad.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.81,0:01:06.73,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,Hmm, not bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.99,0:01:11.39,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,What's the name of the \NBlacksail Fleet's captain again?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.96,0:01:14.30,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,Captain Drake, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.34,0:01:20.78,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,Knight him.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.43,0:01:25.39,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,Give the Blacksail Fleet all \Nthe spoils from this raid.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.39,0:01:28.56,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,I believe Sir Drake and all the \Nwarriors of the Blacksail Fleet
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.56,0:01:31.79,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,will be sincerely grateful for \Nyour generosity, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.43,0:01:36.39,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,Also, Kingfisher replied \Nthat the mission had failed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.73,0:01:40.12,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,She said that the pills were \Nmixed into the wine and drunk.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.12,0:01:44.07,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,However, Prince Roland only \Nslept for a short while, and...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.07,0:01:45.81,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,Failure is failure.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.81,0:01:47.17,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,I don't want to hear excuses.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.17,0:01:48.35,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.30,0:01:51.32,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,Give her one last chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.32,0:01:53.84,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,Send some of her sister's \Nbelongings as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.84,0:01:55.88,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,Let her act accordingly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.88,0:01:56.88,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,You may go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.39,0:01:59.03,Main,Ryan,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.64,0:02:01.60,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,By the way,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.98,0:02:06.54,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,those pills were provided by \NAlchemy Master Enbis, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.08,0:02:09.78,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,What did he say at the time?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.32,0:02:13.31,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,"Dissolves in water. \NDeath upon ingestion."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.42,0:02:16.76,Main,Garcia,0,0,0,,Hang him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.43,0:05:18.91,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The city wall construction \Nis going very smoothly.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.91,0:05:22.13,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Mr. van Bate guarantees \Nit will be completed on time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.13,0:05:23.16,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.16,0:05:24.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,How's trade?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.22,0:05:25.50,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Also going very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.50,0:05:28.88,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The food purchased from \NWillow Town arrived at the docks today.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.88,0:05:31.47,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The exact quantity is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.47,0:05:35.04,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,As you can see, Your Highness, \Nit's enough to see us through the winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.04,0:05:35.99,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.99,0:05:38.14,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,After deducting the cost of buying food,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.14,0:05:39.72,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,we still have a small surplus.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.72,0:05:41.24,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Um, Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.24,0:05:43.23,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,although we have trade income now,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.23,0:05:46.53,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,our fiscal deficit remains \Nextremely severe.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.53,0:05:48.72,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,I'm afraid this isn't \Na long-term solution.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.72,0:05:53.47,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Currently, our main expenditures are \Nall coming from your personal treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.47,0:05:57.78,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,At this rate, it will only last \Nuntil next spring at most.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.78,0:05:58.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.31,0:06:01.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's already very good \Nif we can hold out until then.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.50,0:06:04.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Besides, we still have the ore trade.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.61,0:06:08.05,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,As long as we finish building the wall \Nand secure our foothold in Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.05,0:06:10.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,subsequent ore production \Nwill be guaranteed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.72,0:06:13.86,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,I'm not worried about that, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.86,0:06:19.70,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Duke Ryan won't let it go if we cut off \Nthe ore supply to Longsong Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.70,0:06:21.22,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,What if...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.67,0:06:22.48,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.12,0:06:28.01,Main,Guard,0,0,0,,Your Highness, the Longsong \NStronghold Ambassador has arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.40,0:06:34.10,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov, you said that the food bought \Nfrom Willow Town already arrived, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.10,0:06:35.92,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.92,0:06:40.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Instruct the kitchen to prepare a \Nlavish feast using the delivered food.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.79,0:06:42.71,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Clean the council chamber.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.71,0:06:44.01,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I need to host a guest.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.89,0:07:09.87,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Mr. Hull, please help yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.51,0:07:13.22,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Ah, thank you, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.99,0:07:17.68,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, what are you holding?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.68,0:07:20.14,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh, you mean these?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.14,0:07:21.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I call them chopsticks.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.19,0:07:24.66,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,My people can't afford \Nsilver knives and forks.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.66,0:07:27.80,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But these little wooden sticks \Nare cheap and hygienic.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.80,0:07:29.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The materials are readily available.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.70,0:07:32.45,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I plan to promote them in Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.44,0:07:38.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Of course, there's not much \Ngood food in Border Town right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.34,0:07:40.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'm afraid you'll have to make do.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.00,0:07:42.88,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Oh no, Your Highness, you're too kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.88,0:07:46.35,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Even at the Stronghold, \Nwe don't often get meals like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.61,0:07:49.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This is all to welcome you, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.74,0:07:51.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We don't usually do things like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.36,0:07:54.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,All these ingredients arrived \Nfrom Willow Town today.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.56,0:07:57.71,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Willow Town?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.31,0:07:59.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.70,0:08:02.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Please help yourself, Mr. Hull.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.35,0:08:03.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Don't hold back.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.70,0:08:05.73,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We can discuss business after we eat.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.13,0:08:16.40,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Thank you for your hospitality, \NYour Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.18,0:08:20.39,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,I'm here on behalf of Longsong \NStronghold to inform you that
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.02,0:08:23.53,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,the deadline for the \Nore delivery has passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.53,0:08:27.18,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,The Stronghold has already prepared \Nthe food to be sent to Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.00,0:08:29.10,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.32,0:08:32.39,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,We have yet to receive the ore.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.36,0:08:34.96,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The thing is,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.96,0:08:38.19,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,an unfortunate incident occurred recently.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.12,0:08:41.25,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The northern mine collapsed,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.25,0:08:43.21,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and production stopped for a long time.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.70,0:08:45.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oops, they fell.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.07,0:08:50.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Basically, we can't produce \Nthe agreed quantity of ore.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.93,0:08:53.19,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We only have about two \Nmonths' worth of production.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.19,0:08:54.88,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,I heard about the mine's situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.88,0:08:58.46,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Well then... why not deliver \Ntwo months' worth for now?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.46,0:09:01.12,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The food I'd get in return \Nfor two months' worth of ore
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.12,0:09:02.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,wouldn't be enough to feed my people.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.65,0:09:09.07,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Two years ago, many people in Border Town \Nstarved to death due to food shortages.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.76,0:09:12.28,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I will not allow that to happen again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.52,0:09:16.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This practice of bartering \Nwith the Stronghold...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.93,0:09:19.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,must be abolished.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.52,0:09:23.20,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Ah, Your Highness, you mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.20,0:09:24.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,To be honest with you,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.53,0:09:27.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I have already sold \Nthe ore to Willow Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.02,0:09:30.25,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and bought enough food from them \Nto last through the winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.80,0:09:33.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Not only were they willing to \Nbuy the ore with gold royals,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.43,0:09:36.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,but were also prepared to sell \Nvarious goods at market prices.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.72,0:09:39.82,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Anything that can be bought \Nwith money, they sell.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.82,0:09:40.83,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.43,0:09:44.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Trading with Willow Town is \Nmore advantageous for Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.14,0:09:49.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,They fell again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.30,0:09:55.14,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,So... that explains the ships \Nfrom Willow Town at the dock.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.55,0:10:08.35,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, \NI understand your reasoning now.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.04,0:10:11.69,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,But it seems there are \Na few problems with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.69,0:10:13.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh? Please elaborate.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.70,0:10:17.20,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,To my knowledge, Willow Town \Nhas never traded in ore before.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.20,0:10:19.07,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Even if they pay in currency,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.07,0:10:20.95,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,the price wouldn't be high.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.95,0:10:25.17,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,I think, at most, it would \Nbe half the market price.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.17,0:10:27.14,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,For you, that would be a loss.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.14,0:10:28.87,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,It won't be sustainable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.87,0:10:30.55,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Trade is determined by the market.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.55,0:10:33.27,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Longsong Stronghold has operated in \Nthe Western Region for over a century.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.27,0:10:34.72,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Only a fortress on our scale
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.72,0:10:37.15,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,has the capacity to consume so much ore.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.15,0:10:40.22,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,The Stronghold far surpasses Willow Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.22,0:10:42.42,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,both in development \Nprospects and market size.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.42,0:10:43.57,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,So, in the long term,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.90,0:10:46.22,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Border Town's primary trading partner \Nshould be the Stronghold,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.22,0:10:48.94,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,as that would better serve \Nthe interests of both parties.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.62,0:10:54.64,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Thirty percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.22,0:10:59.18,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,If the Stronghold can purchase \Nore at 30% below market price,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.18,0:11:00.81,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,then it'd be a win-win situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.49,0:11:08.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I've long heard that Petrov Hull of the \NHoneysuckle family is a skilled merchant.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.74,0:11:10.40,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Your reputation is well-deserved.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.88,0:11:13.66,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Thank you for your compliment, \NYour Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.66,0:11:15.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Based on the terms you just proposed,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.74,0:11:18.24,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,it would indeed create \Na win-win situation.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.24,0:11:19.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,However...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.05,0:11:21.59,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Can you guarantee that this will be
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.59,0:11:24.15,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,the unanimous decision of \Nthe Stronghold's Six Families?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.15,0:11:25.02,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.89,0:11:27.41,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,I can't guarantee it 100%,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.21,0:11:30.87,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,but I manage all of the \NStronghold's foreign trade.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.87,0:11:33.52,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,I will do my best to convince \Nthe Duke and the Six Families
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.52,0:11:35.63,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,to accept this mutually \Nbeneficial outcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.49,0:11:41.95,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,I will return to the Stronghold \Nto draft a new contract
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.95,0:11:44.01,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,before visiting Your Highness again.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.01,0:11:47.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Good. Then I shall await \Nyour good news, Ambassador.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.52,0:11:54.31,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.09,0:11:56.66,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,there is one more thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.66,0:11:58.68,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,There are only two months \Nleft until winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.68,0:12:00.53,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Willow Town is quite far away.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.98,0:12:05.82,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,The journey can be dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.77,0:12:10.71,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Therefore, I strongly advise you to \Nconsider certain practical matters,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.83,0:12:14.52,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,from Duke Ryan's perspective.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.01,0:12:16.88,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You misunderstand, Mr. Hull.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.88,0:12:19.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I never planned for my people to \Nspend the winter in Willow Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.00,0:12:22.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Then you mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.11,0:12:23.94,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nor do I plan to go to \NLongsong Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.16,0:12:26.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We're not going anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.34,0:12:30.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This winter, I will build a city \Nwall to defend Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.67,0:12:37.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,making it the new border of \Nthe Kingdom of Graycastle.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.93,0:12:42.40,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.40,0:12:44.49,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,But, Your Highness, \Nlet me say one last thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.49,0:12:47.69,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Your decision affects the fate \Nof everyone in Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.69,0:12:50.09,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,If anything goes wrong, \Nyou have a way out,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.70,0:12:51.75,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,but they do not.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.75,0:12:53.57,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Thank you for your concern, Ambassador.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.57,0:12:56.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I am fully aware of \Nwhat my decision means.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.06,0:12:59.47,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Very well. I have noted \Nall your conditions.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.55,0:13:17.48,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.50,0:13:20.62,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,prepare the food as planned.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.62,0:13:22.14,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.06,0:13:29.05,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.84,0:13:32.06,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,What else did that kid say?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.06,0:13:34.67,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,His Highness said he has \Nalready sold the existing ore
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.67,0:13:37.22,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,to Willow Town in exchange for currency.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.24,0:13:39.31,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Also,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.40,0:13:43.76,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,he has bought enough food for the entire \Ntown this winter from Willow Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.31,0:13:46.06,Main,Nobles,0,0,0,,He did what?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.06,0:13:47.75,Main,Nobles,0,0,0,,What does this mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.75,0:13:48.56,Main,Nobles,0,0,0,,Yeah...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.68,0:13:51.06,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,Anything else?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.51,0:13:54.01,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Also, Prince Roland said that
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.01,0:13:55.48,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,during this year's Months of Demons,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.48,0:13:57.26,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,he won't be seeking refuge \Nat the Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.26,0:13:58.88,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,The people won't leave either.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.88,0:14:01.42,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,His Highness is building a \Ncity wall in Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.42,0:14:03.14,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,He also said...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.66,0:14:05.14,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,What else did he say?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.14,0:14:08.36,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,He also said that he will lead his \Npeople to defeat the demonic beasts
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.36,0:14:09.39,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,and protect Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.39,0:14:14.39,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,making it the new border of \Nthe Kingdom of Graycastle.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.88,0:14:19.11,Main,Noble 1,0,0,0,,What does he think this place is?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.11,0:14:20.39,Main,Noble 1,0,0,0,,Graycastle?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.82,0:14:22.93,Main,Noble 1,0,0,0,,His Highness doesn't think \Nbuilding a city wall
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.93,0:14:24.96,Main,Noble 1,0,0,0,,is the same as playing house, does he?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.96,0:14:28.32,Main,Noble 1,0,0,0,,Piling up a few broken rocks \Nand slapping on some wet mud?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.32,0:14:30.48,Main,Noble 2,0,0,0,,If he built it a bit higher,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.48,0:14:32.39,Main,Noble 2,0,0,0,,it would collapse immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.52,0:14:37.25,Main,Noble 3,0,0,0,,Your Grace, the Prince is bluffing!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.25,0:14:40.00,Main,Noble 3,0,0,0,,Petrov is timid and got tricked by him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.00,0:14:41.46,Main,Noble 3,0,0,0,,We can't fall for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.46,0:14:42.84,Main,Noble 3,0,0,0,,But it's not a bad thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.84,0:14:45.85,Main,Noble 3,0,0,0,,If he fails and flees back \Nto Longsong Stronghold,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.85,0:14:47.86,Main,Noble 3,0,0,0,,he'll naturally be at our mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.86,0:14:49.77,Main,Noble 3,0,0,0,,And if he dies over there...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.77,0:14:51.40,Main,Noble 1,0,0,0,,The farce ends,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.40,0:14:53.52,Main,Noble 1,0,0,0,,and all's well that ends well.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.52,0:14:54.67,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,Boris.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.19,0:14:57.60,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Grace?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.60,0:15:00.77,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,What do you know about the city wall?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.77,0:15:03.60,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Well, Your Grace, a while back,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.60,0:15:06.45,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,that kid was indeed recruiting \Nstonemasons and workers.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.45,0:15:08.42,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,But I thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.42,0:15:11.28,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,I thought he was just renovating \Nhis garden or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.28,0:15:13.78,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,I didn't hear anything about a city wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.66,0:15:26.17,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,Petrov, did you see that city wall?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.17,0:15:29.20,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Before leaving Border Town, \NI specifically went to check.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.20,0:15:32.35,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,On the edge of the Misty Forest, \Nthere were indeed people building a wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.02,0:15:34.78,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,I don't know what method \Nthe Prince is using,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.78,0:15:36.47,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,but construction is proceeding rapidly.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.47,0:15:38.64,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,However, the wall isn't very large.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.64,0:15:42.02,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,In my opinion, it would be difficult \Nto resist the demonic beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.56,0:15:44.02,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,What do you think we should do?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.11,0:16:54.67,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Residents of Border Town!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.40,0:16:59.42,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I am Roland Wimbledon, the Fourth Prince \Nof the Kingdom of Graycastle.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.42,0:17:01.12,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I have gathered you here today
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.12,0:17:04.08,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,because there is an important \Nmatter I must tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.62,0:17:06.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Earlier this morning,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.35,0:17:09.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,the Longsong Stronghold ambassador \Narrived in Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.60,0:17:11.82,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,He came for the ore delivery.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.72,0:17:15.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,As you all know, a month ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.36,0:17:17.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,we suffered an unfortunate accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.60,0:17:20.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The North Slope Mine collapsed,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.11,0:17:23.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and to this day, mining operations \Nhave not fully resumed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.79,0:17:26.63,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We cannot produce enough ore.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.63,0:17:28.46,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I explained the situation \Nto the ambassador,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.46,0:17:30.19,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,hoping he would make an exception
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.19,0:17:33.05,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and give us our winter \Nallocation of food in full.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.60,0:17:35.98,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,However, he refused.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.98,0:17:38.51,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,There was no room for negotiation.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.51,0:17:41.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,He refused to give us our full \Nallocation of food, just like
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.72,0:17:44.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,during the Months of Demons two years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.57,0:17:49.49,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And what's worse, the Graycastle \Nastrologers have told me that
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.49,0:17:52.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,this winter will be longer than usual.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.39,0:17:56.25,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The Months of Demons could last \Nfor more than four months.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.25,0:17:59.90,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That means, if we let things \Nproceed as they are,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.90,0:18:02.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,the tragedy of two years \Nago will repeat itself,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.36,0:18:04.01,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,perhaps even worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.75,0:18:06.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Everyone, please remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.56,0:18:10.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Please remember what \Nwe lost two years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.14,0:18:14.23,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Some of us lost friends,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.23,0:18:15.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,some lost loved ones,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.18,0:18:18.10,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and some lost children.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.56,0:18:19.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This time...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.46,0:18:22.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What more will we have to lose?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.10,0:18:26.32,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What more {\i1}do{\i0} we have left to lose?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.31,0:18:33.08,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,I believe the Prince's move with the \Ncity wall is ultimately about trade.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.66,0:18:35.25,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,His strategy is to advance by retreating.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.25,0:18:39.52,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,His ultimate goal is probably to force us \Nto trade with Border Town using currency.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.52,0:18:43.12,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Prince Roland was sent to govern \NBorder Town due to the Royal Decree,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.12,0:18:44.84,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,so these actions make sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.63,0:18:48.77,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Also, there's no need for a direct \Nconflict with the Graycastle royal family.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.23,0:18:51.33,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,If we can fulfill His Highness's request,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.33,0:18:54.25,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,and purchase ore at 30% below \Nmarket price from now on,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.25,0:18:56.34,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,it would still be a worthwhile deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.34,0:18:59.35,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Furthermore, if he truly \Ncan hold Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.35,0:19:00.77,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,it benefits us as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.77,0:19:04.64,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,First, we can save the enormous expense \Nof fighting the demonic beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.64,0:19:07.94,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Second, the vast lands between \Nthe Stronghold and Border Town
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.94,0:19:09.85,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,could be cultivated and utilized.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.85,0:19:11.76,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,This is all your territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.76,0:19:15.08,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Finally, Prince Roland \Nwon't stay here forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.08,0:19:16.77,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,The Royal Decree lasts only five years.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.77,0:19:19.81,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,In five years, we will have a \Nmore prosperous Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.81,0:19:22.59,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,The people there will \Nstill be your subjects.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.59,0:19:26.47,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,By then, you'll have the third largest \Nterritory in the entire Kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.47,0:19:27.77,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,So my suggestion is that
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.42,0:19:31.40,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,we should, from now on, \Npurchase ore at 30% below market price.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.40,0:19:33.46,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Also, send people to help the \NFourth Prince build the wall,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.46,0:19:35.16,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,and resist the demonic beasts together.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.09,0:19:38.77,Main,Nobles,0,0,0,,Hah! Petrov, you're being far too naive!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.47,0:19:40.77,Main,Nobles,0,0,0,,Are you joking?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.84,0:19:47.77,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,Interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.77,0:19:52.38,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,According to you, this must be another \Nso-called "win-win" conclusion, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.94,0:19:54.74,Main,Petrov,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.40,0:19:58.27,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,The idea isn't bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.03,0:20:02.27,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,But ultimately, it's still \Na merchant's perspective.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.27,0:20:06.09,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,Merchants only see gains \Nand losses, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.61,0:20:08.27,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,Petrov...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.90,0:20:13.21,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,I didn't get to my current position \Nby only considering profits.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.21,0:20:16.77,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,Why would I do business with \Nsomeone I can't control?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.97,0:20:22.41,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,Under my rule, disobey me, \Nand you will be punished.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.41,0:20:26.42,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,As for Border Town, whether it \Nprospers or decays is unimportant.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.42,0:20:29.57,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,What matters is that it's my territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.57,0:20:31.51,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,No one else gets to interfere,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.09,0:20:34.30,Main,Duke Ryan,0,0,0,,not even a Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.28,0:20:38.75,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Everyone, look! This is the food for \Nwinter I purchased from Willow Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.75,0:20:41.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It arrived in Border Town \Nearlier this morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.60,0:20:44.98,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,There's bread, cheese, \Nmead, and dried meat,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.98,0:20:46.57,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,enough for the entire winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.57,0:20:48.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Everyone will be fed.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.27,0:20:50.59,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I swear in the name of Wimbledon:
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.59,0:20:53.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I won't allow the tragedy of \Ntwo years ago to repeat itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.44,0:20:55.27,Main,People,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.27,0:20:58.72,Main,People,0,0,0,,Long live the Prince!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.72,0:20:59.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,However!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.68,0:21:04.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,By doing this, we have essentially \Noffended Longsong Stronghold.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.35,0:21:08.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,They've threatened to stop providing \Nshelter for everyone this winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.27,0:21:11.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I told them that we're not \Ngoing anywhere this winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.68,0:21:13.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We'll stay in our homeland,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.44,0:21:15.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and spend the winter in Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.27,0:21:18.23,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Some of you may have already seen it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.23,0:21:19.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,To the west of Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.60,0:21:22.80,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,a sturdy city wall is \Nsteadily being built.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.80,0:21:26.46,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I know some worry whether we can \Nwithstand the demonic beasts' onslaught.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.46,0:21:28.19,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But let me tell you this:
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.19,0:21:31.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,demonic beasts are no stronger \Nthan ordinary wild animals.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.53,0:21:33.57,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Though they have thick \Nhides and tough flesh,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.57,0:21:36.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,they can't climb walls, \Nand they can't bite through stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.39,0:21:38.49,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,They're nothing but pitiful targets.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.61,0:21:44.21,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I, Roland Wimbledon, Fourth Prince \Nof the Kingdom of Graycastle,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.21,0:21:46.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,hereby issue an urgent call to action.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.89,0:21:48.86,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,All those who can take up arms,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.86,0:21:50.62,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,in order to defend our homeland,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.62,0:21:52.82,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,in order to let us live with dignity,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.82,0:21:55.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,pick up your weapons and join the militia!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.44,0:21:59.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,All militia members will receive \N25 silver royals every month.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.27,0:22:01.23,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If someone unfortunately falls in battle,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.23,0:22:05.15,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,their family will receive five \Ngold royals as compensation.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.15,0:22:08.59,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Tell me, would you rather hide in \Nthe shacks of Longsong Stronghold,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.59,0:22:11.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,pathetically starve to death, \Nand freeze to death without dignity?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.36,0:22:14.82,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Or would you rather follow me and \Nprotect your friends and family,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.82,0:22:17.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,defend Border Town, \Nand defend your homeland
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.39,0:22:19.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,until the final moment?!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.22,0:22:22.04,Main,People,0,0,0,,Defend Border Town!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.86,0:22:34.97,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,You just said the air around us is \Nmade up of many different kinds of gases.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.97,0:22:35.79,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Is that true?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.79,0:22:38.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Of course. Even though \Nthey all look the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.43,0:22:40.79,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, I don't understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.79,0:22:42.24,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,If they all look the same,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.24,0:22:44.23,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,how do you know there are different gases?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.23,0:22:46.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Let me prove it to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.00,0:22:48.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Anna, light this candle for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.85,0:22:50.18,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Oh, sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.17,0:22:57.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If I cover it with this glass jar,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.44,0:22:59.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,do you know what will happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.43,0:23:02.75,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Um, the flame will go out.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.25,0:23:05.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And why will the flame go out?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.93,0:23:08.84,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Because the air inside the jar is used up.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.91,0:23:13.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You mean, because there's \Nno air left in the jar,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:13.00,0:23:14.42,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,that's why the flame goes out?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.42,0:23:15.82,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.82,0:23:19.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana, pour that limewater \Nover there into this basin.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.53,0:23:21.43,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Oh! Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.00,0:23:27.23,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Now, let's take a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.23,0:23:30.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If I lift this jar, \Nwhat do you think will happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.93,0:23:38.61,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Ah! This is...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.61,0:23:40.41,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If there was nothing in the jar,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.41,0:23:42.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,we wouldn't see bubbles or \Nchanges in the water surface.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.35,0:23:45.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This proves that air contains \Nat least two different gases.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.84,0:23:49.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,In fact, the candle only consumes \Na part of the air as it burns.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.74,0:23:52.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The other part cannot \Nparticipate in combustion,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.35,0:23:54.14,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and also turns the limewater cloudy.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.14,0:23:55.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Although they're both \Ncolorless and odorless,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:55.84,0:23:57.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,they have completely different properties.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.34,0:23:59.55,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,So that's how it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.55,0:24:01.04,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,But what's the use of knowing all this?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:01.04,0:24:03.66,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,If we use the first gas alone,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.66,0:24:05.35,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,we can make the flame burn brighter.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.88,0:24:07.62,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,And the second type of gas
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.62,0:24:09.54,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,can extinguish the flame quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.35,0:24:12.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Well said.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:12.50,0:24:14.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Ever since humans learned to use fire,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.36,0:24:16.17,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,we've set ourselves apart from animals.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:16.17,0:24:18.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And its origin might \Nhave been an accident,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.34,0:24:20.14,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,perhaps lightning striking a tree,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.14,0:24:23.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,or sparks from stones colliding \Nthat ignited a flame.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.35,0:24:25.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But if no one had noticed this,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.53,0:24:27.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,if no one had tried to harness it,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.27,0:24:29.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,we might still be no different \Nfrom beasts today.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.35,0:24:31.25,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This experiment is meant to show you that
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.25,0:24:34.16,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,curiosity and thinking are the \Ndriving forces of human progress.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.16,0:24:37.21,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,You've just been in the rain. \NHave some hot water, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.21,0:24:38.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Thank you, Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.35,0:24:41.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,In fact, there are many such \Npotential forces in nature
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.27,0:24:42.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,waiting for us to discover and use them.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:42.85,0:24:45.55,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,They may seem insignificant, \Nbut when harnessed together,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.55,0:24:47.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,they can produce astonishing power.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.74,0:24:50.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I believe the power of \Nwitches is the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.32,0:24:52.86,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's all for today's lesson.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:52.86,0:24:55.38,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter, you're responsible \Nfor taking Nana back.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:55.38,0:24:56.47,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.47,0:24:57.74,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Goodbye, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.67,0:25:01.20,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Anna, you should also \Ngo back and get some rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.20,0:25:02.47,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Thank you, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.05,0:25:05.67,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh, by the way, Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.67,0:25:06.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Did you confirm it?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:06.72,0:25:08.45,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Are the Snow Powder and \Nice that I requested
Dialogue: 0,0:25:08.45,0:25:10.21,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,in the shipment that arrived \Nfrom Willow Town today?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.21,0:25:11.81,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Oh, yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:11.81,0:25:13.47,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I've already had someone check.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.47,0:25:16.37,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,But why do you need \Nso much Snow Powder and ice?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.37,0:25:18.10,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,We don't have any celebrations right now,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.10,0:25:20.05,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,nor anything that needs to be kept cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.62,0:25:24.26,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,For the next experiment.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.51,0:26:27.47,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Don't move.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:30.89,0:26:32.68,Main - Top,CREDITS,0,0,0,,Translator: Henry Lin\NTimer: Henry Lin\NEditor: Zachary Carlysle\NQC: William Haggard
